      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "Both GND1 (pin 4) and GND2 (pin 5) of the isolated CAN transceivers U10 and U11 are connected to the same GND net.",
      "expected": "GND1 (logic-side ground) and GND2 (isolated bus-side ground) should be on separate nets to maintain galvanic isolation, as required by the isolated CAN transceiver part and the specification's 'isolated CAN buses'.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "GND [High Power] : ... U10.4(GND1,power_in) U10.5(GND2,power_in) U11.4(GND1,power_in) U11.5(GND2,power_in) ..."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (CAN0, CAN1), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller (U8, U9) through an isolated CAN transceiver (U11/companion)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The isolation between the logic side and the CAN bus side is defeated, so the CAN buses are not isolated. This can cause ground loops, loss of common-mode rejection, and potential damage, contrary to the intended design.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["J1", "Module1", "U11", "D10", "R34", "J2", "J13"],
      "pins": ["J1.15", "Module1.200", "U11.6", "D10.1", "R34.1", "J2.8", "J13.8"],
      "nets": ["/CAN0_N"],
      "observed": "The /CAN0_N net includes J1.15 (HDMI SCL) and Module1.200 (HDMI0_SCL) in addition to the expected CAN0_N pins (U11.6, D10.1, R34.1, J2.8, J13.8).",
      "expected": "J1.15 and Module1.200 should be on a separate HDMI0_SCL net, not connected to the CAN0_N bus.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "/CAN0_N : D10.1(Input,input) J1.15(SCL,passive) J13.8(Pin_8,passive) J2.8(Pin_8,passive) Module1.200(HDMI0_SCL,open_collector) R34.1(1,passive) U11.6(CANL,bidirectional)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The CAN0 bus is shorted to the HDMI DDC clock line, which will prevent both interfaces from functioning and may cause contention or damage.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["D4", "D14", "D23"],
      "pins": ["D4.2", "D14.2", "D23.2"],
      "nets": ["/LED_3.3V_POWER_SW"],
      "observed": "The net /LED_3.3V_POWER_SW contains only the anodes of D4, D14, and D23 (pins 2) and has no connection to any power source or driver.",
      "expected": "The anodes should be connected to a 3.3V power source (e.g., +3V3 or a switched 3.3V rail) so the LEDs can operate.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "/LED_3.3V_POWER_SW : D14.2(A,passive) D23.2(A,passive) D4.2(A,passive)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The LEDs D4, D14, and D23 will never light because their anodes are floating.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain multiple anomalies, most notably the isolated CAN transceivers have their logic and bus grounds tied together, defeating isolation, and the CAN0_N bus is shorted to the HDMI DDC clock. Additionally, the anodes of three status LEDs are left floating."
}

